      "questionId": "q0",
      "value": "q0_pay_when_roi_clear",
      "rationale": "As a busy dual-income parent, I'm pragmatic about tools. I'd test the free tier to see if it actually reduces my calendar chaos and stress. Once I confirm it saves me time and eliminates missed deadlines, I'd happily upgrade to Plus.",
      "confidence": 0.88
    },
    {
      "questionId": "q1",
      "value": "q1_happy_plus_or_pro",
      "rationale": "If the core Plus features (digest, handoffs, 6 members) solve my fragmentation problem, the extra $5 for email parsing is worth considering. I'd evaluate Pro once I'm comfortable with the platform, but I'm not rigid about which tier.",
      "confidence": 0.82
    },
    {
      "questionId": "q2",
      "value": "q2_annual_after_long_use",
      "rationale": "I'm cautious about locking in money upfront, especially for a new app. I'd want 2–3 months of sustained daily use before committing to an annual plan. Once I'm confident it's indispensable, annual pricing makes sense.",
      "confidence": 0.85
    },
    {
      "questionId": "q3",
      "value": "q3_one_dollar_try_cancel",
      "rationale": "A $1 trial month is low-friction and worth testing. I'd use it to see if Plus genuinely improves my family coordination. If it doesn't deliver obvious value, I'd cancel and stay on free.",
      "confidence": 0.86
    },
    {
      "questionId": "q4",
      "value": "q4_compare_pay_if_wins",
      "rationale": "I'm not obsessive about free alternatives, but I do compare options quickly. If FocusLoop clearly outperforms what my friend uses—especially on the family-specific features—I'd pay. I'm results-driven, not price-driven.",
      "confidence": 0.84
    },
    {
      "questionId": "q5",
      "value": "q5_ads_pay_if_plus_useful",
      "rationale": "Ads are annoying, but they're not my primary reason to upgrade. I'd pay for Plus if the handoffs, digest, and shared calendar deliver real value. Ad-free is a nice bonus, not the driver.",
      "confidence": 0.83
    },
    {
      "questionId": "q6",
      "value": "q6_fair_if_use_justifies",
      "rationale": "At $6.99–$11.99/month, FocusLoop is reasonably priced for a family coordination tool. I'd view it as fair if it genuinely reduces my stress and eliminates missed deadlines. The value is in the outcome, not the absolute cost.",
      "confidence": 0.87
    },
    {
      "questionId": "overall_interest",
      "value": 4,
      "rationale": "This product directly addresses a real pain point in my household: scattered notifications and missed events. The weekly digest and task handoffs appeal to me. I'm not giving it a 5 only because I want to validate it works before full commitment.",
      "confidence": 0.86
    },
    {
      "questionId": "would_try_beta",
